# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: snow mana payment for an activated ability cost.
# Forcing: Ascendant Spirit's first activation requires exactly {S}{S}; two Snow-Covered Islands are the only usable sources.
# AI behavior: the AI has no meaningful decisions; the script drives the activation and stack resolution.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN   = the client can offer, pay, and resolve a snow-mana activation.
#   LOSE  = not expected; no opposing pressure exists.
#   TIMEOUT = activation offer/payment/priority wiring failed.
# Card roles:
#   Ascendant Spirit -- source of the {S}{S} activated ability.
#   Snow-Covered Island -- snow sources that produce blue mana with snow-source metadata.
# Protocol path: ActionsAvailableReq Activate + manaCost Snow, ActivateMana payment options with FromSnow.

[metadata]
Name:Snow Mana Ascendant Spirit
Goal:None
Turns:3
Difficulty:Easy
Description:Activate Ascendant Spirit's {S}{S} ability using two Snow-Covered Islands.

[state]
ActivePlayer=Human
ActivePhase=Main1
